SECTION | KEY | VALUE
------------------------------
# rooms.pdl - gta-hq rooms and doors. Same row shapes as @.apps/pet-trainer/rooms.pdl (ROOM / DOOR), in TILE units instead of pixels. Every DOOR is a teleport: the door picture sits on the wall row at tx,
# the trigger cell is the floor cell right below it (tx,2); touching it (INT arrow step, or an auto=1 autonomous walk) teleports to dest at arrive_x,arrive_y.
# ROOM | id | name | floor_col | floor_row        floor tile = Inside_A5 col,row (48 px tiles)
# ROOM may carry a 6th column "outdoor": an outside room (sky from the RPG Maker parallaxes by game time - day CloudySky1, dawn/dusk Sunset, night StarlitSky - grass and a path from Outside_A5, a house wall with the door).
# SCENERY | room | sheet | col | row | w | h | x | y     fixed RPG Maker tiles that block walking and furniture (trees, flowers, a well)
# DOOR | room | tx | dest | arrive_x | arrive_y | auto      auto=1: the pet may walk to this door by itself; auto=0: only you send it (INT)
# gta-hq (2026-10-12): ONE island city (an OVERMAP room: a world-map biome, tiles scaled to 32 px, island on a square ocean) + the five building interiors. Room kinds: normal (13 x 8 cells of 48 px with a wall strip), outdoor, over.
# ROOM | id | name | floor_col | floor_row | over | cols | rows | tile_px | biome      (the overmap biome "worldmap" = World_A1 ocean + World_A2 sand/grass; the buildings are World_B tiles in SCENERY rows; later biomes: desert, snow ...)
# DOOR | room | tx | dest | arrive_x | arrive_y | auto | ty    ty = the row of the door object (default 1 = the wall strip); its trigger is the cell below it. City doors sit on the building, the pet arrives next to the trigger.
ROOM | city   | City         | 0 | 0 | over | 20 | 13 | 32 | worldmap
ROOM | castle | Castle       | 3 | 4
ROOM | bank   | Bank         | 1 | 4
ROOM | store  | Store        | 1 | 2
ROOM | school | School       | 0 | 2
ROOM | hotel  | Hotel        | 2 | 4
